# Laid by gavel, regenerable by the next order — never this repo's source. These
# three used to reach a newborn through `furnace ignite`, which appended them at
# birth (`ensure_gitignore`); the applier lays and appends nothing, so the
# template says it instead. The base store keeps one blob per laid file so the
# next order can tell a hub move from a local edit.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.furnace/base/

# Tool-poured surfaces: laid down at stamp time and regenerable by the tool that
# poured them, so they are not this repo's source. `.specify/` comes from
# `specify init` (a copier task); `.claude/` from furnace. The gate never reads
# either.
#
# .specify/ was tracked anyway across 42 repos -- 1,005 files, ~24 each -- which
# was never a decision anybody wrote down: only .specify/feature.json was ignored,
# while .claude/ was ignored wholesale. Same category, opposite treatment.
#
# An existing repo needs `git rm -r --cached .specify` as well; a gitignore rule
# does not evict what is already in the index.
.claude/
.specify/

# Agent session locks. .claude/hooks/agent_lock.py writes .agent-locks/<session>.json
# at SessionStart and unlinks it at SessionEnd; a dead pid's lock is reaped on the
# next read. Per-machine runtime state keyed to a live pid — worthless to any other
# clone, meaningless once the process exits. The machine-global excludes file carries
# this for clones that already exist; the template is what makes a newly stamped repo carry
# it on its own.
.agent-locks/
